From 78822c0e48ade43d3c7323e167ddcd12c7956a21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:27:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 55/55] drm/gma500: add an sgxfive register snapshot to debugfs

Work on an open microkernel needs the closed firmware's register state
before and after each kind of job, to compare with later. The status file
shows only seventeen registers and prints the firmware words eight to a
line, so two dumps do not diff well.

Add dri/N/sgx/regs: the 191 registers the firmware reaches with ldr and
str (tools/usse-dis/regtouch.py over the microkernel), the 21 the host
uses on its own (event enable, BIF fault and request status, the sixteen
directory lists), then HostCtl, TA3DCtl and the kernel CCB control words,
one value a line under a versioned header. The 21 registers whose write
starts work (VDM, ISP and render starts, event and PDS cache clears, PDS
invalidates, DPM allocate, free, store/load and out-of-memory commands)
are listed but never read. The file only reads, under the device lock.

KUnit checks the table (sorted, aligned, 191 firmware and 21 host
registers, the 21 skipped ones), that a capture reads each other register
once and never a skipped one, and the text.

Assisted-by: LLM
